ed in TypeScript

Copyright (c) 2026 wordgitet
SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD

tsed is a real implementation of the classic ed line editor in TypeScript,
running on Bun.  That sentence is also the joke.

This is a research toy, not a claim of complete POSIX conformance.  It targets
POSIX platforms only.  Windows is not supported.

Building and running

Install Bun and build the editor from the repository root:

    bun install
    bun run build

The build creates two command names:

    ./dist/ed
    ./dist/tsed

Both accept the following arguments:

    ./dist/ed [-s] [-p prompt] [--] [pathname]

The minimum usable Bun version is not known.  Development currently uses Bun
1.3.14, so trying an older version is at your own risk.

A tiny session

Run the editor:

    $ ./dist/ed -s

Then enter:

    a
    hello, world
    .
    s/world/POSIX/
    p
    Q

The editor prints:

    hello, POSIX

The a command appends input until a line containing only a dot.  The s command
substitutes text, p prints the current line, and Q quits without a
modified-buffer warning.

Where to go next

TOUR is the complete guided presentation of the editor.  It explains the
architecture, command language, limitations, and runnable examples.

CONTRIBUTING.md explains development, validation, style, and the AI disclosure
policy.
